cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Galpi, its experiment data or its specification, please cite it as below and link to the repository."
title: "Galpi: AI-native codebase navigation for coding agents"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jason
    alias: jasonwpgml
repository-code: "https://github.com/jasonwpgml/galpi"
url: "https://github.com/jasonwpgml/galpi"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-21
abstract: >-
  Galpi is an experimental navigation layer that keeps coding agents such as
  Claude Code and OpenAI Codex from getting lost in a codebase. It improves
  code structure upstream and adds a compact machine-readable index (.gp files)
  only for what code cannot express: task state (done, work in progress, plan,
  dead, locked), intent and routing from task aliases to the minimal set of
  files. Rules for dead and locked code are enforced by a PreToolUse hook,
  pre-commit and CI rather than by prompt compliance. The repository includes a
  TypeScript CLI (galpi check, doctor, build, query), an A/B experiment harness
  and measured results from more than 350 isolated agent runs: a compact index
  cut total tokens by 16.6 to 20.3 percent against verbose docs on Codex, hook
  gating shrank Claude Code's token overhead from 12.1 to 1.9 percent, and on a
  1,300-line fixture improved structure alone was cheaper than any index on
  both agents. Experiment write-ups and the spec draft are CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - coding agents
  - ai agents
  - claude code
  - codex
  - codebase navigation
